---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';

const story = {
  company: 'PayFit',
  logo: '/images/customers/testimonials/payfit/logo.png',
  person: {
    name: 'Alain Hazout',
    role: 'VP Sales',
    photo: '/images/customers/testimonials/payfit/person.jpeg'
  }
};
---

<MainLayout
  title="PayFit Customer Story - How Pipeline Visibility Transformed Sales Reviews"
  description="Learn how PayFit's sales team uses Pyko to maintain pipeline accuracy, improve forecast reliability, and transform business reviews."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="gradient-hero py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <nav class="mb-8">
          <a href="/customers" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white transition-colors text-sm">
            Customers
          </a>
          <span class="text-gray-600 mx-2">/</span>
          <span class="text-white text-sm">PayFit</span>
        </nav>

        <!-- Company Logo -->
        <div class="mb-8">
          <div class="inline-block px-6 py-4 rounded-xl bg-white">
            <img
              src="/images/customers/testimonials/payfit/logo.png"
              alt={story.company}
              class="h-10 w-auto object-contain"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Headline Quote -->
        <blockquote class="text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-8 leading-tight">
          "Starting to use Pyko was a game changer for us. We went from confrontational business reviews to a smooth pipeline."
        </blockquote>

        <!-- Author Info -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <img
            src={story.person.photo}
            alt={story.person.name}
            class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-white/20"
          />
          <div>
            <p class="text-white font-semibold">{story.person.name}</p>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">{story.person.role} at {story.company}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Stats -->
  <section class="py-12 bg-white border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-8 text-center">
          <div>
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold" style="color: #F94730;">20+</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Active automations</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold" style="color: #F94730;">200+</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Sales reps using Pyko</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold" style="color: #F94730;">90%+</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Close date accuracy</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold" style="color: #F94730;">5 hrs</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Saved per rep per week</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story Content -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none" style="color: #374151;">
          <h2 style="color: #061A35;">The Challenge</h2>
          <p>PayFit, a leading European payroll and HR SaaS company, had a familiar problem: a fast-growing sales team struggling with CRM data quality. With 200+ sales reps across multiple countries, keeping Salesforce data accurate was a constant battle.</p>
          <p>Business reviews were becoming confrontational. The CRO couldn't trust the forecast because close dates were outdated, pipeline stages didn't reflect reality, and critical fields were empty. Managers spent hours manually reviewing pipelines before every meeting.</p>

          <h2 style="color: #061A35;">The Solution</h2>
          <p>PayFit implemented Pyko to bridge the gap between Salesforce and Slack, where their team already spent their day. The rollout focused on three areas:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Close date hygiene:</strong> Automated alerts for deals with past close dates, with one-click "Push 30 Days" buttons</li>
            <li><strong>Pipeline visibility:</strong> Real-time notifications when deals hit critical stages, ensuring managers always have an up-to-date view</li>
            <li><strong>Data quality enforcement:</strong> Cleaning rules that flag missing next steps and incomplete fields on a daily basis</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 style="color: #061A35;">The Results</h2>
          <p>Within weeks of deploying Pyko, PayFit saw immediate improvements:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Close date accuracy jumped to 90%+</strong> - Reps now keep dates current because updating takes one click in Slack</li>
            <li><strong>Business reviews transformed</strong> - From confrontational to constructive, because everyone trusts the data</li>
            <li><strong>Forecast reliability improved</strong> - Clean data means accurate forecasts, which means better business planning</li>
            <li><strong>Rep productivity increased</strong> - Less time updating CRM, more time selling</li>
          </ul>

          <blockquote style="border-color: #F94730;">
            <p>"Starting to use Pyko was a game changer for us. We went from confrontational business reviews because we couldn't trust the forecasts to a smooth pipeline."</p>
            <cite>- Alain Hazout, VP Sales at PayFit</cite>
          </blockquote>

          <h2 style="color: #061A35;">Why PayFit Chose Pyko</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Speed of deployment:</strong> Live in minutes, not months</li>
            <li><strong>Salesforce + Slack integration:</strong> Meets reps where they already work</li>
            <li><strong>One-click actions:</strong> Eliminates the friction of CRM updates</li>
            <li><strong>Affordable pricing:</strong> Works for a team of 200+ without enterprise contracts</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Features Used -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-8 text-center" style="color: #061A35;">Features PayFit uses</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <a href="/product/live-alerts" class="block p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
            <h3 class="font-bold mb-2" style="color: #061A35;">Live Alerts</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Real-time deal stage notifications in Slack</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/product/cleaning-rules" class="block p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
            <h3 class="font-bold mb-2" style="color: #061A35;">Cleaning Rules</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Automated data quality enforcement</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/product/actions" class="block p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
            <h3 class="font-bold mb-2" style="color: #061A35;">One-Click Actions</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">CRM updates directly from Slack</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    headline="Get the same results as PayFit"
    subheadline="Start your free 14-day trial. Setup in under 5 minutes."
    primaryCTA={{ text: "Start Free 14-Day Trial", href: "/trial" }}
    secondaryCTA={{ text: "See All Customer Stories", href: "/customers" }}
    variant="gradient"
  />
</MainLayout>
